{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1504566-in-your-opinion-is-mage-too-attached-to-real-life-politics","id":1504566,"title":"In your opinion is Mage too attached to real life politics??","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-03-06T04:01:22-08:00","id":1504566,"title":"In your opinion is Mage too attached to real life politics??","content":"For the record, i am NOT referring to things like gender, race, sexuality, etc, at least for the purpose of this thread . I am not even necessarily talking about M20 per se. Rather, i am talking about the very way the game is structured.<br /> <br /> <br /> For instance, what is the single most hated tradition in Mage? Not by players, but rather &quot;which one has a lot of bad things written about it&quot;<br /> I think the answer is, obviously, the Order of Hermes. My issue is not, for instance, that the order has politics, or is hypocritical, or evil or whatever. What bothers me is that all of this is presented<br /> from a very OOC perspective. Read guide to the sabbat , to the Camarilla, the Dharma books, or whatever. You will always find the group in question representing itself, so to speak, along with<br /> some more neutral, cold, &quot;clinical&quot; input from the writer.<br /> <br /> Should you own the books, please just read some literally random pages from &quot; clanbook Tremere revised&quot; and Order of hermes Revised, to mention just one of a myriad of examples spread through countless books. <br /> It is as if i am reading a history pamphlet written by either the Hollow Ones, or at the very least, the most reform-minded in the Order. In essence, they are portrayed as bumbling idiots with the word &quot;pride&quot; given as a justification.<br /> <br /> Now, there are 2 possibilities here. 1) the writers hate Hermeticism as a concept. I think this one can be safely discounted.<br /> 2) The order represents all the RL things hated by the writers It all but screams<br /> &quot;This is the Washington/Democratic establishment. These are the people representing the bad history of western civilization &quot;<br /> Note: whether or not this is true is besides the point. The main issue is that they are presented as such even from their own freaking perspective. Last i checked, the Republican party Platform,<br /> was written by the actual Party, right?<br /> <br /> I focused on the order, because it is, in my opinion. the easiest example to analyze, but you can see this, to a lesser or greater extend, with the other Traditions, albeit with more subtlety<br /> That is, in general, the more sympathy the writers have towards any particular group, the more positively it will actually be presented even from an IC perspective. In short, the more the<br /> people representing the &quot;establishment&quot;* hate, say, the Euthanatoi , the more you know that they will actually get a very good portrayal. (which is not necessarily a bad thing, depending on <br /> how it manifests in the writing, mind you).<br /> <br /> *Establishment here meaning the people that your mage is supposed to be railing against. Yes, it's not explicitly stated, and i suppose i could be wrong, but i think that it short of is, in a &quot;taken for granted&quot; kind of way, in a fashion that i do not see in, say, Vampire, which does not take for granted your character's ideology in relation to his Sect.<br /> <br /> <br /> This whole situation reminds me of a DnD joke &quot;All drow characters are rebels against their evil kind...which no one ever actually sees.&quot;<br /> Except that in DnD this seems accidental( player choice), rather than the way it is presented.<br /> <br /> This would also lead to the question of whether or not mages should be represented as more amoral, on average, but i would probably be threadjacking my own thread, lol<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-06T06:09:17-08:00","id":1504583,"title":"","content":"Wouldn't know really, my overall perception of the Order of Hermes, Tremere origins and middle ages WoD is more strongly colored by Ars Magica and some small references in 1st ed. books than anything connected to 2nd ed, Ascension, Dark Ages or - gods forbid - Sorcerer's Crusade.<br /> <br /> The moment some genius decided tried to throw that &quot;Doissetep began as an Akashic center somewhere in Asia&quot; angle back in the original Book of Chantries, i decided that any and all Ascension lore from that point onwards should be taken with a roman legionary's whole monthly pay of salt.<br /> <br /> <br /> In fact in my own chronicles/personal headcanon i make an active point of considering DA:V and Sorcerer's Crusade settings as <b>NOT</b> really parts of the true actual past of WoD at all but a weird spirit/dream realm derived from a sub-section of the Malkavians' Cobweb and an alternate timeline generated by massive Time Paradox, respectively.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 03-06-2023, 09:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-06T06:30:07-08:00","id":1504584,"title":"","content":"Oh absolutely. It's necessary to remember that all those games were created in the 90's, and with that era mentality. Werewolf the Apocalypse is the most 90's environmentalist fantasy of &quot;revenge of mother nature&quot;. Vampire is a cynical view of the elites, and Mage is absolutely a criticism against the government, but not just any government, it's against the US government and upon which every possible conspiracy theories are driven into overdrive. Funny how the game didnt took the same consideration in criticizing the communist dictatorships of the USSR or China thou, who were 10.000 times worse and are comparable to Nazi Germany heh? <br /> <br /> Those 3 games (as well as Changelling and Wraith as well) are horror games (personal horror), and as horror games, each is based in some kinds of fears. Good horror stories always deal with some of our fears. Werewolf for instance deals with fear of nature, obviously, which is one of our most basic fears, but also fear of disease and fear of filthy (the whole fomori thing is based on our fears of filthy and diseases, which are closely connected). Vampire deals with fear of death and fear of blood (blood is also connected to death, and is also a very basic fear we have). Wraith deals with the fear of death obviously, as well as fear of the unknown, but Mage is interesting because while it does deal with the fear of the unknown - which is a basic fear for little scared monkeys as us humans - the central theme and the focal point of the fear is another: it is the <b>fear of the government.</b><br /> <br /> Mage deals with the fear we all have of being waked up in the middle of the night by masked men dragging us out of our homes and disappearing forever. That's a particularly important fear in the West, exactly because we enjoy some degree of freedom, and therefore we are afraid to lose it, while in countries like Russia or China people simply shut their mouths and obey exactly for being afraid.<br /> <br /> So yes, those games are definitely too political, although way too simplistic in their worldviews","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-06T08:49:40-08:00","id":1504592,"title":"","content":"thin of it this way. one of the central tenets of the game's settings is that if enough people believe in something,it becomes true. keeping that in mind,how could it not be poliitical?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 03-06-2023, 12:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-06T09:48:04-08:00","id":1504597,"title":"","content":"To be fair mage has been really rough to the order of hermes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-06T10:12:25-08:00","id":1504605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1504566-in-your-opinion-is-mage-too-attached-to-real-life-politics?p=1504597#post1504597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair mage has been really rough to the order of hermes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm speculating of course, but maybe the way they wrote the Order of Hermes was a preventive measure to avoid accusations of favoritism. They caught a lot of that with the Tremere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-06T10:23:43-08:00","id":1504609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The writers hate Hermeticism as a concept </div> </div> </div>You say that this can be safely discounted but, I'm not so sure. I wonder how much did Brucato set as a precedent for that kind of thing. Brucato being infamous for being anti-structure and anti-modernization, so I wouldn't put it past that Brucato, maybe unintentionally, wrote hatred of Hermeticism into the system.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12895-mrnatas","name":"MrNatas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12895_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-06T10:42:53-08:00","id":1504612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1504566-in-your-opinion-is-mage-too-attached-to-real-life-politics?p=1504584#post1504584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh absolutely. It's necessary to remember that all those games were created in the 90's, and with that era mentality. Werewolf the Apocalypse is the most 90's environmentalist fantasy of &quot;revenge of mother nature&quot;. Vampire is a cynical view of the elites, and Mage is absolutely a criticism against the government, but not just any government, it's against the US government and upon which every possible conspiracy theories are driven into overdrive. Funny how the game didnt took the same consideration in criticizing the communist dictatorships of the USSR or China thou, who were 10.000 times worse and are comparable to Nazi Germany heh?<br /> <br /> Those 3 games (as well as Changelling and Wraith as well) are horror games (personal horror), and as horror games, each is based in some kinds of fears. Good horror stories always deal with some of our fears. Werewolf for instance deals with fear of nature, obviously, which is one of our most basic fears, but also fear of disease and fear of filthy (the whole fomori thing is based on our fears of filthy and diseases, which are closely connected). Vampire deals with fear of death and fear of blood (blood is also connected to death, and is also a very basic fear we have). Wraith deals with the fear of death obviously, as well as fear of the unknown, but Mage is interesting because while it does deal with the fear of the unknown - which is a basic fear for little scared monkeys as us humans - the central theme and the focal point of the fear is another: it is the <b>fear of the government.</b><br /> <br /> Mage deals with the fear we all have of being waked up in the middle of the night by masked men dragging us out of our homes and disappearing forever. That's a particularly important fear in the West, exactly because we enjoy some degree of freedom, and therefore we are afraid to lose it, while in countries like Russia or China people simply shut their mouths and obey exactly for being afraid.<br /> <br /> So yes, those games are definitely too political, although way too simplistic in their worldviews</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Vampire may be a cynical view of elites, but it is presented from a very cold and detached perspective. That is, it seems to be realistic in its portrayal of how power works, albeit heavily<br /> exaggerated by the realities of being a vampire(such as the fact that your bosses will never retire). Had it been written like mage, however, it would have basically said &quot;here's how your anarch players can change things, because of course you will be an anarch&quot;<br /> <br /> For instance, i have to admire whomsoever wrote &quot;guide to the sabbat&quot;. You can sort of see his personal disgust at sabbat behavior, but he still presented them from their own perspective.<br /> These are the Sabbat. This is what they believe. Now here's some OOC commentary to make you see past the propaganda. The same is true for literally every splatbook and &quot;clan&quot; book i have ever read on every gameline .<br /> Basically, it is subtle. Sort of like a poem that 10 different students can interpret however they like, even if, technically, the writer did mean one single &quot;thing&quot;<br /> <br /> Except for mage! In mage, the only traditions that get this nuanced treatment are those that the writers tend to like on a personal real life level, or even better, those that they neither like nor dislike.<br /> For instance, the aforementioned OOH can easily be seen as representing white entitlement, western elitism, imperialism, some level of racism etc. All of these things are true, but all their chapters<br /> are written from someone who, to put it mildly, is not the order's golden boy<br /> In essence, when playing werewolf, i get the impression that a werewolf is talking to my character<br /> When reading Order of Hermes revised, i get the impression that the writer is telling me his politics in an extremely crude sort of way<br /> Vampire will tell you &quot;here's what the elders did&quot; Mage will tell you &quot;Here's what the shitlords masters who rule us did&quot;<br /> In Vampire you see the opinions of Vampires. In mage you see the RL opinions of writers explicitly written<br /> Take, for instance Clanbook Lasombra. Does anyone actually believe that the writer was a social darwinist??? I sincerely doubt it.<br /> Imagine how it would look like had it been written in the way that mage is.<br /> Again, it's not just the Order that gets this treatment. It is simply the most obvious example.<br /> When i see the mages 90s establishment, i literally see the Bill Clinton administration. When i see it collapse, i can short of hear the writer wishing that it happens in real life.<br /> Whether or not this should have happened is besides the point. The point is that any and all subtlety is missing<br /> <br /> By the way, even werewolf was a lot more nuanced, for the most part, than mage. Things were presented from an actual werewolf perspective. From what i recall tribebook red talons contained<br /> opinions about humanity that were downright genocidal. And yet, SOME effort was taken to present them from their own POV<br /> Book of the weaver basically says you &quot;would it not be nice if the weak were culled and left to die&quot;?<br /> These are not the writer's own opinions. It is supposed to acclimate you into playing a garou while also filling you, the player, with horror due to the knowledge that your fomori slashing hero<br /> probably believes things that would mean some very unfortunate implications about you, personally.<br /> Mages lacks a filter. Perhaps this is the word i am looking for.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Again, i am not against mentioning things like racism, homophobia, etc This is an entirely separate thing. Although, even there, i would argue that they are presented from an extremely simplistic and historically wrong perspective.<br /> For instance, modern day racism is a relatively recent thing. Europeans did not participate (en masse, anyway,) in the African slave trade until the 16 century. The Americas were &quot;discovered&quot;<br /> decades after the council was formed. And yet, supposedly the mages were ahead of their time in being racist to the dreamspeakers. Fuck, apparently they even chose their name for them.(at least i think this is what m20 implies. I could be wrong)<br /> Because that's what you do if you gain leverage over someone. You use it to choose their name.<br /> And remember, that you had centuries old masters who were used to a feudal medieval perspective. Quite &quot;progressive&quot; of them to be more racist than even the sleepers of the time were.<br /> Also, apparently, in 1750 half the native americans left the council because some hermetic decided to be bad against them. Like, it is so cartoonishly simple, and ironically enough, racist, implying that this is how politics work. Hint : they don't.<br /> It's one thing to say that mages are not immune to racism. It is another, entirely, to imply that they are driven by it to such a monomaniacal extend.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrNatas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1504566-in-your-opinion-is-mage-too-attached-to-real-life-politics?p=1504609#post1504609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You say that this can be safely discounted but, I'm not so sure. I wonder how much did Brucato set as a precedent for that kind of thing. Brucato being infamous for being anti-structure and anti-modernization, so I wouldn't put it past that Brucato, maybe unintentionally, wrote hatred of Hermeticism into the system.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> If i am not mistaken, and i could be, wicca takes a lot from Hermetic believes. That is, i doubt any of the writers hate, say, neoplatonism or the spiritual aspects<br /> of Alchemy,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1504566-in-your-opinion-is-mage-too-attached-to-real-life-politics?p=1504605#post1504605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm speculating of course, but maybe the way they wrote the Order of Hermes was a preventive measure to avoid accusations of favoritism. They caught a lot of that with the Tremere.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI assume you are referring to the fact that the Tremere signature character has nearly enough discipline dots to start tanking methuselahs? lol.<br /> <br /> The thing is that because the OoH is a relatively secular organization, as well as very well organized, it makes perfect sense to portray them as more corrupt<br /> than average. Its easy to avoid politicos when you have literally zero internal hierarchy, after all. This is not the issue. The issue is that everything about the order, and the traditions in general, was written by <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Mark_Hallward_Gillan\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Mark_Hallward_Gillan</a> <br /> <br /> this guy. Lol. As well as his fellow in-tradition progressives. (again, i know i am repeating myself a lot, but i am NOT talking about things like gender, race, etc<br /> After all, i imagine even corrupt Caeron Mustai was probably not a member of the local evangelical church trying to undo voting rights, lol<br /> The same goes about the Traditions in general. Imagine if there was a pro elders party and an anti elders party.<br /> In Vampire, it is not presumed that you will choose one or the other. You may go anarch, autarkis, fucking inconnu(long shot but whatever), sabbat, or you may pay your dues and one day fill the elder's shoes. It will merely cost you everything you once were.<br /> <br /> In mage, it is kinda presumed that you are a member of the anti-elders party, unless you really, really want otherwise, and you really shouldn't<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","user":"mark","date":". 03-06-2023, 01:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-06T11:33:31-08:00","id":1504615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1504566-in-your-opinion-is-mage-too-attached-to-real-life-politics?p=1504612#post1504612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If i am not mistaken, and i could be, wicca takes a lot from Hermetic believes. That is, i doubt any of the writers hate, say, neoplatonism or the spiritual aspects<br /> of Alchemy,</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't say that is wrong but, if my understanding of Brucato is correct I also would say it doesn't matter. Without getting to much into the weeds, Brucato whole thing is more about the liberation people through the returning to nature <i>basically</i>. So regardless of what wicca takes influence from, if its not doing sex magic in the woods while worshipping the Mother Goddess then it might be looked down on.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12895-mrnatas","name":"MrNatas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12895_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-06T12:19:02-08:00","id":1504619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1504566-in-your-opinion-is-mage-too-attached-to-real-life-politics?p=1504612#post1504612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In mage, it is kinda presumed that you are a member of the anti-elders party, unless you really, really want otherwise, and you really shouldn't</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and this is very well represented by one quote of Porthos from one of the oldest books of Mage (I think it's the oldest novel?), the Fragile Path: <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">&quot;Vitality is siphoned from us with age. Even if we slow the advance within our bodies, we cannot keep the weight from our enlightened minds. The more we see, the more we think we know. The more we believe we understand, the more set in our ways we become, and the more we limit our potential. Thus, youth is the flame that ignites the future. Power is merely polish on blunted blades&quot;</td> </tr> </table></div> And can be seen trought such things as the numerous, numerous, instances of repeating that ascencion isn't about power, and that Spheres are a trap of sorts. The one character that I know that supposedly Ascenced, was a very young mage. And I don't know any Master+ that's described as Ascended<br /> <br /> This one may be one of the few themes ALL of Ascencion agrees on.<br /> <br /> But I'm not sure how this theme being so important enters into real-life politics, or more sprcificly, I'm not convinced that it's a direct consequence of Mage being more politicaly loaded than Vampire. Rather, the premise it's less Gothic:<br /> <br /> In Vampire you can chose to be Anarch, but really the war of the ages it's untenable: You *know* that the Elders are going to win. Even if your character has hope and plans a lot, and manages to succeed many times, you *know* that hope ends with Gehena, with the Antediluvians awakening, and there's less than a hail mary chance of stopping this.<br /> <br /> In Mage the idea it's more like you actually *can* win the war of the ages. Power it's less constrained by age, some of the strongest of the old guys are actually on your side, etc...(then Revised came, and practically won the &quot;war&quot; for u :P)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 03-06-2023, 03:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-06T13:17:05-08:00","id":1504627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1504566-in-your-opinion-is-mage-too-attached-to-real-life-politics?p=1504619#post1504619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, and this is very well represented by one quote of Porthos from one of the oldest books of Mage (I think it's the oldest novel?), the Fragile Path: <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">&quot;Vitality is siphoned from us with age. Even if we slow the advance within our bodies, we cannot keep the weight from our enlightened minds. The more we see, the more we think we know. The more we believe we understand, the more set in our ways we become, and the more we limit our potential. Thus, youth is the flame that ignites the future. Power is merely polish on blunted blades&quot;</td> </tr> </table></div> And can be seen trought such things as the numerous, numerous, instances of repeating that ascencion isn't about power, and that Spheres are a trap of sorts. The one character that I know that supposedly Ascenced, was a very young mage. And I don't know any Master+ that's described as Ascended<br /> <br /> This one may be one of the few themes ALL of Ascencion agrees on.<br /> <br /> But I'm not sure how this theme being so important enters into real-life politics, or more sprcificly, I'm not convinced that it's a direct consequence of Mage being more politicaly loaded than Vampire. Rather, the premise it's less Gothic:<br /> <br /> In Vampire you can chose to be Anarch, but really the war of the ages it's untenable: You *know* that the Elders are going to win. Even if your character has hope and plans a lot, and manages to succeed many times, you *know* that hope ends with Gehena, with the Antediluvians awakening, and there's less than a hail mary chance of stopping this.<br /> <br /> In Mage the idea it's more like you actually *can* win the war of the ages. Power it's less constrained by age, some of the strongest of the old guys are actually on your side, etc...(then Revised came, and practically won the &quot;war&quot; for u :P)</div> </div> </div> </div>In retrospect, i should have given a different name to this thread. I meant it in the sense of &quot; Do the RL politics of the writers affect the way the actual traditions are presented, based on whether or not the groups represent something that the writer(s) hate in a way that is simply not there in any other gameline?&quot; So i guess the fault is mine for not clarifying it.<br /> If you need any comfirmation, go read say. the order of hermes books and compare them with,say, the euthanatos or dreamspeakers books.<br /> <br /> Yes, ascension is not about power. But this says nothing about the way the books are written<br /> <br /> Take clanbook Nosferatu for instance. Now imagine if it was ALL said from the perspective of a Cleopatra embraced like 5 months ago. Then the same Cleopatra also wrote like literally everything Nosferatu and Camarilla related in Vampire.<br /> <br /> And this, is exactly how the establishment is presented.<br /> <br /> <br /> Think of Transcendence in wraith the oblivion. Actually, some mage books literally imply its the same thing<br /> You are not going to transcend by climbing the Hierarchy's ranks, but damn it, it's still an option. That is, the Hierarchy is (unless i am remembering it wrong), written from the Hierarchy's own perspective plus some neutral anti-propaganda commentary by the writers as well as dissending opinions<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT. Just to clarify I am not implying that the relationship between elder mates and younger ones need be as antagonistic as they are in vampire. The reasons for this conflict are simply not there. Quite the opposite in fact. It's part of the reason I do not quite find things like the horizon <br /> war as particularly plausible. A bad copy of vampires elder <br /> Neonate conflict if you ask me <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","user":"mark","date":". 03-06-2023, 04:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-06T13:28:12-08:00","id":1504631,"title":"","content":"Nope. I think one can argue that early Mage ran the risk of charicature, and that is a thing that casts a shadow over the entire franchise, but on the whole, the attachment to politics is one of the things that makes it richer and stronger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-06T13:51:26-08:00","id":1504636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1504566-in-your-opinion-is-mage-too-attached-to-real-life-politics?p=1504631#post1504631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope. I think one can argue that early Mage ran the risk of charicature, and that is a thing that casts a shadow over the entire franchise, but on the whole, the attachment to politics is one of the things that makes it richer and stronger.</div> </div> </div> </div>In retrospect, I regret naming the thread as I did, but I believe<br /> I clarified I was not referring to things like race, gender, sexuality, etc. Mages are less divorced from normal humans than vampires so it kinda makes sense. I do have an issue with the crude way they are presented, but the main subject is the &quot;style&quot; the books are written. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> For the record I am gay, kinda androgynous looking and a bit neuroatypical, so I assure you this thread is NOT meant to be <br /> a stealthy way of saying that I hate gays <br /> <br /> Perhaps there is some better way for me to articulate my points, but if so I can not think of any","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-06T13:53:13-08:00","id":1504637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1504566-in-your-opinion-is-mage-too-attached-to-real-life-politics?p=1504636#post1504636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In retrospect, I regret naming the thread as I did, but I believe<br /> I clarified I was not referring to things like race, gender, sexuality, etc. Mages are less divorced from normal humans than vampires so it kinda makes sense. I do have an issue with the crude way they are presented, but the main subject is the &quot;style&quot; the books are written.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> For the record I am gay, kinda androgynous looking and a bit neuroatypical, so I assure you this thread is NOT meant to be<br /> a stealthy way of saying that I hate gays<br /> <br /> Perhaps there is some better way for me to articulate my points, but if so I can not think of any</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't say anything about that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-06T13:55:58-08:00","id":1504638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1504566-in-your-opinion-is-mage-too-attached-to-real-life-politics?p=1504637#post1504637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I didn't say anything about that?</div> </div> </div> </div>A misunderstanding on my part then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-06T14:03:37-08:00","id":1504640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1504566-in-your-opinion-is-mage-too-attached-to-real-life-politics?p=1504584#post1504584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh absolutely. It's necessary to remember that all those games were created in the 90's, and with that era mentality. Werewolf the Apocalypse is the most 90's environmentalist fantasy of &quot;revenge of mother nature&quot;. Vampire is a cynical view of the elites, and Mage is absolutely a criticism against the government, but not just any government, it's against the US government and upon which every possible conspiracy theories are driven into overdrive. Funny how the game didnt took the same consideration in criticizing the communist dictatorships of the USSR or China thou, who were 10.000 times worse and are comparable to Nazi Germany heh?</div> </div> </div> </div>Rage Across Russia and Book of Wyrm.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-07T03:49:32-08:00","id":1504744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrNatas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1504566-in-your-opinion-is-mage-too-attached-to-real-life-politics?p=1504615#post1504615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wouldn't say that is wrong but, if my understanding of Brucato is correct I also would say it doesn't matter. Without getting to much into the weeds, Brucato whole thing is more about the liberation people through the returning to nature <i>basically</i>. So regardless of what wicca takes influence from, if its not doing sex magic in the woods while worshipping the Mother Goddess then it might be looked down on.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I just don't get this, though. I do not understand what led to this. You'd think, for instance, that the people who wrote, say, guide to the Camarilla, guide to the Sabbat, Dharma book devil tigers, etc, are also against the behaviors described within.<br /> After all, none of the writers was ever accused of carrying big black blood-stained bags in the middle of the night, right?* And they all had some little sidebars &quot;you are not a serial killer, or if you are, please get help&quot; written in the books<br /> <br /> So, i don't get why this is missing in the Mage books. It's as if the entire Ventrue book was written by the tiny Ventrue anarch minority.<br /> Or imagine if a member of the Green party was asked to write the Libertarian party platform, and its political positions from his own perspective. (I just chose two random parties mind you)<br /> So the &quot;abolish the income tax&quot; is still there, but with a &quot;helpful&quot; &quot;and here's how these egomaniacal quasi-sociopathic rand fanboy shitheads would run the economy, so please don't vote for them!&quot; Or, at the very least, it is as if the Party Platform was written by outsiders within the party.<br /> <br /> The problem is not that the Traditions have an establishment made up of, uhm , &quot;not the best people around&quot;. It is the freaking WoD. I would have been weirded if their politics were not like that.<br /> <br /> The problem is that the entire line is written down from their opposite perspective<br /> For instance, it is not a coincidence that, say, the ecstatic signature character belongs to the faction that would be closest, ideologically, to the writers. Note, i am not saying every/most/ or even many of the signature characters should not be anti-establishment. This is not a problem. The problem is that every word is written from that perspective. Every in-character word. Every OOC word.<br /> In essence, Mage was the only game* that presumed what kind of character you were going to play, beyond what was enforced by the metaphysics and societal structures of the game. <br /> <br /> Again, even ignoring things like race and gender. For the purposes of this entire thread, let us assume that even the most corrupt master is pro lgbt and anti-racist.<br /> Would this have changed more than a few sentences in the books? No, because the problem is structural<br /> <br /> Ironically enough, i like DA: Mage a lot more, precisely because this problem is absent. <br /> Anyone who owns DA mage grimoire can verify this by reading any random chapter about the fellowships. It is written from a fashion that is a lot more clinical and detached<br /> Oh sure, you can see some comments being harbingers of future events, but the same can be said in how Guide to the High clans wrote the Brujah. It provides logical context for future events<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> On a side-note, how are the Traditions presented in Victorian age Mage? I am not asking whether its full of a shitty establishment. But, at the end of the day, did the establishment of the day<br /> even bother to have a propaganda budget?<br /> <br /> <br /> * Ok maybe mummy too, but there are like a tiny handful of mummies, made by specific people, of specific people etc so it's not illogical.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-07T07:36:58-08:00","id":1504757,"title":"","content":"There's a certain irony to this, considering that <b>Mage</b> is, more than any other <b>WoD</b> game, at least ostensibly about exploring philosophical diversity. One would think that it would be the gameline that makes the <i>most</i> effort to present different perspectives without passing judgment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-07T14:29:07-08:00","id":1504781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1504566-in-your-opinion-is-mage-too-attached-to-real-life-politics?p=1504612#post1504612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Vampire may be a cynical view of elites, but it is presented from a very cold and detached perspective. That is, it seems to be realistic in its portrayal of how power works, albeit heavily<br /> exaggerated by the realities of being a vampire(such as the fact that your bosses will never retire). Had it been written like mage, however, it would have basically said &quot;here's how your anarch players can change things, because of course you will be an anarch&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>So, basically 5th edition?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Except for mage! [+stuff] </div> </div> </div>I cant disagree here. Mage was basically written as fighting the &quot;good fight&quot; against Bill Clinton and Bill Gates from the 90's. It is... Somewhat childish in the way it was written. It is a game about cringe edgelords &quot;fighting the system&quot;, quite literally. I mean, I absolutely love the 1984 / Brave New World Illuminati whackos of the Technocracy, and turning cyborgs and genengineered aliens on dragons and fairies and fighting fireballs with lasers is delicious, but yes, Mage is rather simplistic, and hey Im an Ancap, so I already consider the State to be the enemy of the people. But they gave several cartoonishly depictions of the factions - and yes I agree, most of what it is about the OoH is rather silly and just turn them and the techies into moustache twisting villains","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-07T15:23:13-08:00","id":1504782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1504566-in-your-opinion-is-mage-too-attached-to-real-life-politics?p=1504757#post1504757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a certain irony to this, considering that <b>Mage</b> is, more than any other <b>WoD</b> game, at least ostensibly about exploring philosophical diversity. One would think that it would be the gameline that makes the <i>most</i> effort to present different perspectives without passing judgment.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really think that the entire problem resides around the theme chosen for the games. Vampires are the cynical elites, so they are ALL garbage - which allowed the writters to dump upon themselves in a sort of detached way. &quot;Lets just present the worse hedonistic and corrupt behaviors we can think about the RL elites that we can&quot;. Werewolf is all about mother nature vs &quot;evil capitalism&quot; - actually against evil &quot;industrial world&quot;, but &quot;evil industrial world&quot; in the 90's is basically &quot;evil capitalism&quot;. So it's monsters fighting cartoonish moustache twisting villains, so again it's easier to be more detached.<br /> <br /> Also, the writters of this games are a bunch of shallow hippies, let us be honest here. Like somebody above mentioned, anything except doing sex in the woods and worshipping mother nature was bad for those new age guys. So they had no problems about shitting on humanity, and when you say about ideas like the Red Talons being genocidal or the Weaver believing that the weaklings should be &quot;culled&quot;, and when you say that the authors dont believe that... Well, you know... Im not so sure brother.<br /> <br /> On a personal note, my father is a marxist communist, and when those people say that they are all about love and sunshines... I gotta tell you, that sort of people do have pretty genocidal ideas. Ever heard about &quot;Neo Malthusianism&quot;? It's the idea that &quot;Mother Earth&quot; has too many people around, and that is a sort of idea that is absolutely LOVED by those New Age hippies types. And how do you think that &quot;overpopulation&quot; can be solved? Yeah, right.<br /> <br /> So, every time I would read about &quot;too many humans&quot; on the WtA games, I would IMMEDIATLY get the hint of the writters that they would PERSONALLY love to have a good old genocide to &quot;reduce the overpopulation&quot;.<br /> <br /> So no, I absolutely do NOT believe that they DO NOT believe in those ideas.<br /> <br /> About Mage however, Mage is a game that got itself a lot closer to real life than the other games, which is why it got a lot more political. First of all, Mages are the most humane of the critters of WoD, in every possible sense. They represent the pinnacle of humanity, for better or worse; Mages dont have a cursed thirsty for blood, nor an unnatural lunacy (from &quot;Luna&quot;, the Moon) to turn into a killing monster or any other sort of alien weirdness.<br /> <br /> Mages also represent the Hegelian idea (urgh, Hegel, another bastard, and the worse of all who caused all the crap of the 20th century) that cultures and nations are &quot;conducted&quot; by exceptional individuals - because of course, peasants are shit. &quot;The masses&quot; of sheep that blindly follow some &quot;Enlightened&quot; asshole. As such, each Mage represents the &quot;ubermensch&quot; of their respective culture, the Nietzschenian &quot;superman&quot; of each culture, no exceptions.<br /> <br /> Therefore, the game basically wrote itself into being something upon which the writters could dump their RL politics upon. Yes, Ventrue are assholes, but they are just stereotypical &quot;generic&quot; elites. A Ventrue could, in theory, represent either a Washington bureocrat but also a japanese Daymio. A Toreador could be a generic decadent Hollywood producer.<br /> <br /> But for Mage it's different. The Traditions are <b>culture based</b>, particularly 1ed. Therefore, the Chorus is the evil Catholic Church, the OoH is the evil medieval feudalism. The Verbena are good thou, because they are having orgies in the woods under the full Moon and they are &quot;fighting the system&quot;.<br /> <br /> And the Technocracy, oh boy, those guys are the absolutely worse, they are evil incarnated with no redeemable traits. Those guys are the Washington bureaucrats, the billionaires and their FBI and CIA and NSA lapdogs, they are the worst! The &quot;pig capitalists&quot;, and therefore you should never ever ever want to be them, and Im 100% that the writters regreat having write the Guide to the Technocracy and Im also 100% that they are actually appalled that so many people love them (lets remember, the Union was NOT supposed to be playable on the 1st edition)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-07T18:31:59-08:00","id":1504803,"title":"","content":"Kakost - Please stop attacking and insulting the original creators of the gamelines. You don't know them, nor what they were thinking when they created the works that led to decades of folks having fun and internet arguments, and your extrapolations regarding them are not necessary in discussing those game books. Please keep your discussion about the work, not made-up suppositions as to what a varied and constantly changing group of creators were &quot;really&quot; like. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-08T05:22:35-08:00","id":1504834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RichT</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1504566-in-your-opinion-is-mage-too-attached-to-real-life-politics?p=1504803#post1504803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kakost - Please stop attacking and insulting the original creators of the gamelines. You don't know them, nor what they were thinking when they created the works that led to decades of folks having fun and internet arguments, and your extrapolations regarding them are not necessary in discussing those game books. Please keep your discussion about the work, not made-up suppositions as to what a varied and constantly changing group of creators were &quot;really&quot; like. Thanks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah yes, the powers to be never appreciate being insulted by the peasants.<br /> <br /> Gotcha boss. I'll self censor myself from now on - wouldnt want to insult the lords of the game and get myself in a tough spot.<br /> <br /> After all, who cares about what the peasants think right? What matters is what the CEO wants.<br /> <br /> You got it boss, Im shutting my mouth right now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-08T14:28:56-08:00","id":1504880,"title":"","content":"A self described ancap (who also sees themself as a peasant?) complaining about a private owner policing the behavior of consumers who have concensually decided to exist on a forum they privately manage to discuss the owners product is the most on brand thing I've seen in a long time.<br /> <br /> I was pretty cynical about where this thread would go, but this definitely took the cake. Like of course Mage is political. Of course it's focused on particular coalitions and forms of pluralistic politics. It was never about diversity and inclusion to all worldviews. It was about underdogs and the strange allies, like the Order of Hermes, they form in resisting hegemony. Sure it doesnt have the most coherent political analysis, but hey if you want to reconcile real political tensions maybe just do that in your life or homebrew it. If someone could make a game based in a setting tangentially based on reality focused on the politics of knowledge and reality that is not polarizing they are either naive or have figured out a way of aligning political projects that warrants a Nobel peace prize.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-08T16:01:14-08:00","id":1504881,"title":"","content":"I think another part of Mage which complicates any political reading is that the territory which Mage is working in, that late 20th century occult mileau, while you can certainly argue that in relation to society it has political significance, within its own internal boundaries it abstracts itself significantly from the material foundations from which actual politics is drawn.<br /> <br /> Which isn\u2019t to say that the means of organizing the factions of Mages isn\u2019t interesting or that considering how they and Magick might relate to society in general isn\u2019t interesting, but it\u2019s also difficult to comfortably synthesize politics as such with the abstract realms of consciousness and mystery that occultism is naturally concerned with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-08T23:56:34-08:00","id":1504909,"title":"","content":"One of the things a mate of mine noticed is that mage factions don't really mimic irl politics in ways we'd expect. For example the nine Mt's are very individualistic vs the collectivist Union. One of the things I noticed about the disparate crafts is at least one is hard right wing","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-09T05:45:31-08:00","id":1504928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1504566-in-your-opinion-is-mage-too-attached-to-real-life-politics?p=1504597#post1504597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair mage has been really rough to the order of hermes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why? They are just a group of highly intellectual mages with a pragmatic utopian ideal. I.E. if everyone is a Mage and has a solid education poverty won't exist. And forms of government based on coercion won't be viable. <br /> <br /> I grant you the Order acted like Europeans of their periods. But, ask yourself, how did non-Europeans of those periods act?<br /> <br /> If the various other traditions were written to reflect the real world behavior of people from their cultures, we likely hate everyone but the Etherites and the Adepts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-09T05:59:01-08:00","id":1504929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1504566-in-your-opinion-is-mage-too-attached-to-real-life-politics?p=1504928#post1504928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why? They are just a group of highly intellectual mages with a pragmatic utopian ideal. I.E. if everyone is a Mage and has a solid education poverty won't exist. And forms of government based on coercion won't be viable.<br /> <br /> I grant you the Order acted like Europeans of their periods. But, ask yourself, how did non-Europeans of those periods act?<br /> <br /> If the various other traditions were written to reflect the real world behavior of people from their cultures, we likely hate everyone but the Etherites and the Adepts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes if everyone was highly educated and had incredably privilege then then poverty wouldn't exist. Exactly. For example of we work towards unified cohesive theorem of magic we could ensure every has equity.<br /> <br /> Awful, For example the euthanatos feel very comfortable playing judge, jury and executioner.<br /> <br /> correct.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 03-09-2023, 12:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-09T06:01:22-08:00","id":1504930,"title":"","content":"Mage has an important similarity to Science Fiction. It is always hungry for ideas. Any ideas that can't escape get thrown in. This would make a game written by apolitical authors seem political. And Mage wasn't created by apolitical people. So everything got dumped in that was in the area of Mage's authors. We will need to cut them some slack for that.<br /> <br /> What we need is better handling of viewpoints forward. Having a Hollow One blast the Order of Hermes for causing the &quot;Whitemare&quot; is one thing. Never having an Hermetic call the Hollow Ones on their smug elitism is another. We need a sense of conflicting viewpoints and values. After all, Mage is about changing the world. And that is always political.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-09T08:12:48-08:00","id":1504938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1504566-in-your-opinion-is-mage-too-attached-to-real-life-politics?p=1504928#post1504928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the various other traditions were written to reflect the real world behavior of people from their cultures, we likely hate everyone but the Etherites and the Adepts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why do you exclude the Etherites and Adepts? Victorian Mage points out how both factions started out with problematic elements, too. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-09T08:42:02-08:00","id":1504942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1504566-in-your-opinion-is-mage-too-attached-to-real-life-politics?p=1504938#post1504938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why do you exclude the Etherites and Adepts? Victorian Mage points out how both factions started out with problematic elements, too.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It just seems to me that they would be the least obviously obnoxious people in the room. If everyone else is a major league jerk, you can be pretty rude and still come off as the sweet one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-09T09:22:26-08:00","id":1504946,"title":"","content":"It's very easy to overly identify with mages. Vampires are an elite beyond the elite, werewolves are radicals beyond radicals, but mages are just people with ideas and strong egos. Moreso, people have this particular political weakness: Economic policies (Vampire) and environmental protections (werewolves) are put on the backburner before Identity politics (Mage) despite the former being far more important to governance than the latter. <br /> <br /> Also like, it's pretty natural to have strong reactions when Mages are literally making bullshit work. Homeopathy, herbal remedies, chiropractors, acupuncture, raki... It's infuriating that people IRL make a living from these practices, siphoning funds and time from people who need real medical attention, now imagine there's a chosen people that actually can make the BS work. That's maddening.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-09T14:00:32-08:00","id":1504973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1504566-in-your-opinion-is-mage-too-attached-to-real-life-politics?p=1504946#post1504946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's very easy to overly identify with mages. Vampires are an elite beyond the elite, werewolves are radicals beyond radicals, but mages are just people with ideas and strong egos. Moreso, people have this particular political weakness: Economic policies (Vampire) and environmental protections (werewolves) are put on the backburner before Identity politics (Mage) despite the former being far more important to governance than the latter.<br /> <br /> Also like, it's pretty natural to have strong reactions when Mages are literally making bullshit work. Homeopathy, herbal remedies, chiropractors, acupuncture, raki... It's infuriating that people IRL make a living from these practices, siphoning funds and time from people who need real medical attention, now imagine there's a chosen people that actually can make the BS work. That's maddening.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, i had not considered that. Yeah, i guess that identity politics do feel a lot more &quot;visceral&quot; than,say, last year's budget. So, it's possible that this made writers less likely to constrain themselves? After all, here you have these people representing beliefs that have been hurt in real life. And there you have some people (e.g the septarians and other conservative choristers) representing the ones that have done the hurting. Of course, some books will mention that few magical paradigms are a direct copy of real life beliefs, but it seems like this detail was observed more as an exception than as a rule. So, to sum it up :<br /> <br /> 1) what was written above<br /> <br /> 2) Mages are biologically humans, thus, the writers feel less of a need to &quot;stay in character&quot; Since, you are not portraying something that merely masquerades as human, it becomes more of a temptation to just assume that, say, the Traditions are the Democratic party, but with superpowers, not just as an accidental approximation, but as a very direct/crude analogy<br /> <br /> After all, it did not seem to me that any writer (though i could be wrong), cared about &quot;the reestablishment of Sidhe rule over the commoners after a 400 year old absence, reinvigorating feudal bonds&quot;. Because it is so out of &quot;here&quot; and &quot;now&quot;<br /> On the other hands, books describing the Horizon wars and its aftermaths seem like someone's wish list for the 90s/early 2000s. Its as if someone really wished the green party had won the election. Its as if, the more Bill Clinton was reaching the heights of his political power, the more the establishment was trashed in Mage.<br /> Nevermind that said conflict in Mage, technically had nothing to do about, say, the 1996 welfare reform<br /> \u200bThey do not feel like, say, a Kindred/changeling/wraith historian making a carefully edited commentary. They all but shout &quot; Here's what i would have supported, had i been a Mage&quot;<br /> <br /> 3)By the way, at least Vampire gives a HUGE list of reason for the elder/neonate conflicts. Mage fails to do the same. And yet, going by many books, this conflict is replicated to a huge extend.<br /> (No, disciples do not have anywhere near as bad as young vampires. Not even as an approximation)<br /> <br /> One almost get the impression that certain books were written under a huge fear that people might actually, god forbid, support the establishment. Something that would have been very much tolerable in, say, any other of whitewolf games. Its as if someone was scared to hell that people who roleplay establishment characters in Mage, might end up voting the wrong way in real life.<br /> <br /> Actually, a lot of Mage seems to have been written under the impression that if you play a bad character (especially one who is human), you might end up doing bad things.. Not unlike, how some people thing that your behavior in GTA will influence your real life lol. You can see that some of,say, the infernalist books were written by writers who had to be forced kicking and screaming to do so. One wonders whether they would have had the same opinion of, say, writing a Sabbat book. I mention this, because, ironically enough, these books ended to being written as more &quot;in character&quot; Perhaps because even mage writers felt silly saying &quot;skinning people alive is bad&quot; every second paragraph. After all, no one runs on such a platform in any of the USA representative districts (that i know of, anyway lol).<br /> <br /> It gets worse in that the bad people are also portrayed as bumbling idiots. For instance, the Taftani would, in a sense, be seen as representing magical terrorism. They do not care if you like their paradigm (i.e politics) , only that you &quot;believe&quot; it. So, they are portrayed as, well, psychotic. Then again, i suppose i should be happy that they did not end up in a literal &quot;antagonist&quot; section.<br /> I mention the taftani to clarify that its not just a Hermetic thing.<br /> <br /> So the end result is that mages are basically political activists. They may be bad because they do extreme actions (e.g pogrom) in the name of their political ideals. They may be corrupt like,say, the Democratic Leadership council (whatever its name). It almost feels like magic is anciliary to the whole thing. Wouldn't magickal powers be a huge temptation to people? (no, showing just the extreme of the Nephandi does not suffice). Wouldn't some mages, say start feeling bad towards sleepers whose presence literally maintains paradox?<br /> To clarify, i am not saying that the average Mage should be the uhm sabbat, that's kinda stupid. But right now it feels they are all basically fundraisers for political causes, not merely out of brutal<br /> necessity (i,e altering the consensus), but out a nearly 100% held belief (other than the aforementioned establishment) that their way is the right way of creating absolute Utopia.<br /> <br /> I am not saying that the philosophical conflict should be taken out entirely, just to be clear. After all the creation of,say, the Order of reason only or mostly makes sense for the sake of actually helping people, but as it stands, i find it, and all the above points elements that are used to crudely<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-09T15:01:17-08:00","id":1504981,"title":"","content":"There <i>is </i>a tendency in Mage to treat the various factions as stand-ins for real-world politics, something that other gamelines would get pilloried for doing. Part of that is that Mage is about \u201cwhat people believe\u201d, in a way that no other World of Darkness gameline is. So when the Victorian Mage Order of Reason is said to be behind that era's colonialism, the tendency is to view it as \u201cthe 19th century Order of Reason is a reflection of the real-world colonialist tendencies of that era\u201d, not as \u201chey! Victorian Mage is saying that this magickal conspiracy was the <i>real </i>source of the atrocities of the Victorian era; not cool!\u201d By contrast, consider the trouble the folks at Paradox got into early in the development of Vampire 5e when one of their first supplements essentially claimed that some of the atrocities taking place in\u2026 Afghanistan, I think? were actually the result of the schemes of an elder vampire. <br /> <br /> That said, the associations aren't one-to-one. As much as some may think it is, the Technocracy <i>isn't</i> a stand-in for \u201cthe vast Right-Wing Conspiracy\u201d; it's a stand-in for an overly authoritarian government. Progressives tend to think of that as a right-wing thing; conservatives tend to think of it as a left-wing thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-10T06:14:31-08:00","id":1505015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1504566-in-your-opinion-is-mage-too-attached-to-real-life-politics?p=1504981#post1504981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, the associations aren't one-to-one. As much as some may think it is, the Technocracy <i>isn't</i> a stand-in for \u201cthe vast Right-Wing Conspiracy\u201d; it's a stand-in for an overly authoritarian government. Progressives tend to think of that as a right-wing thing; conservatives tend to think of it as a left-wing thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>In fairness <b>[Redacted]</b> is correct and <b>[Redacted]</b> is far more authoritarian. [<b>Redacted]</b> may make the same claim, but they are just projecting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1504566-in-your-opinion-is-mage-too-attached-to-real-life-politics?p=1504981#post1504981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So when the Victorian Mage Order of Reason is said to be behind that era's colonialism, the tendency is to view it as \u201cthe 19th century Order of Reason is a reflection of the real-world colonialist tendencies of that era\u201d, not as \u201chey! Victorian Mage is saying that this magickal conspiracy was the <i>real </i>source of the atrocities of the Victorian era; not cool!\u201d\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>The flip side of this is that Mage factions tend to get painted as being for whatever the readers think the group they represent is for, baggage and all. No one blinks an eye at magical healthcare and faith healing in Dungeons and Dragons. In Mage, the factions that practice strange medicine tend to get lumped in with quacks and con artists even though the Mages can make it work and are trying to make it work for everyone. In a similar way the Technocracy is often painted as wanting high healthcare costs or global warming or other anxieties of the modern world, when that is not necessarily true (it might be, but only if it makes for a good story).<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-10T06:40:46-08:00","id":1505016,"title":"","content":"And ultimately, that's the main point: the single biggest thing that M20 got right was \u201cit's your game; do with it as you will\u201d. How well it follows up on that idea is an open question; but it at least acknowledges the <i>principle </i>that it isn't the devs' jobs to tell you how to run your game. Earlier editions, not so much.<br /> <br /> That <i>does</i> mean that there will be gaming groups that use Mage in ways that will make the game's writers tear their hair out; but frankly, that's <i>always</i> been true. To the extent that they follow that principle in M20, it's a lot healthier than trying to dictate something that they ultimately can't control anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-10T08:16:56-08:00","id":1505018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1504566-in-your-opinion-is-mage-too-attached-to-real-life-politics?p=1505015#post1505015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The flip side of this is that Mage factions tend to get painted as being for whatever the readers think the group they represent is for, baggage and all. No one blinks an eye at magical healthcare and faith healing in Dungeons and Dragons. In Mage, the factions that practice strange medicine tend to get lumped in with quacks and con artists even though the Mages can make it work and are trying to make it work for everyone. In a similar way the Technocracy is often painted as wanting high healthcare costs or global warming or other anxieties of the modern world, when that is not necessarily true (it might be, but only if it makes for a good story).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's quite correct and it's been something I wanted to point out before the topic spun out of control. Mage is a perfect mirror to hold up against ourselves and our perceptions of the World.<br /> <br /> Mage is about belief, faith and fighting for them. There is a core conflict between freedom, autocracy and destructive nihilism presented through a punky lens that claims that the youth will make it all better... Until they turn into the old.<br /> <br /> Everything else is brought to the table by the people discussing and playing the game. It's not a mirror of our world, it's a mirror of ourselves.<br /> <br /> This is also what makes diacussing mage incredibly infuriating because half the time you are not really discussing mage - you are discussing your own ethics and worldviews and when people disagree with you on those you end up arguing.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-10T12:44:58-08:00","id":1505033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1504566-in-your-opinion-is-mage-too-attached-to-real-life-politics?p=1504981#post1504981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, the associations aren't one-to-one. As much as some may think it is, the Technocracy <i>isn't</i> a stand-in for \u201cthe vast Right-Wing Conspiracy\u201d; it's a stand-in for an overly authoritarian government. Progressives tend to think of that as a right-wing thing; conservatives tend to think of it as a left-wing thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Weirdly as a left winger I tend to percieve it as left wing. If anything this makes it more scary rather than less.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-10T13:16:34-08:00","id":1505036,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m currently of the mind that, when it comes to the Union v. The Council, it\u2019s less a matter of a distinction between left and right and more a question of what the Status Quo ought to be and what our relationship to that Status Quo ought to be. I could also maybe see an argument for a authority-liberty axis being a point of distinction.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t think those are a perfect allegory either, because as I\u2019ve mentioned above, I think the concepts of Mage are too concerned with the occult worldview to be readily translated into material politics, but I do think there\u2019s enough of a case to be made in either case. I do tend to think that a simple left-right binary (already a somewhat frought conception IMO) isn\u2019t the best way of illustrating the Union or the Council. As has been noted, both factions are portrayed in a wide enough fashion to contain either left or right elements within them.<br /> <br /> Ultimately though, I think that even rubrics that are generally appropriate don\u2019t particularly hold up under the scrutiny and the setting as presented. One could argue that the main distinction between the Union and Council is whether they choose to uphold or break with the predominant paradigm (the status quo). However it also must be noted that there have been elements of the Union who are not satisfied with other Union interpretations of said paradigm and how it ought to be advanced, this being an underlying cause for any Technocrat Civil War.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-10T13:56:31-08:00","id":1505041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1504566-in-your-opinion-is-mage-too-attached-to-real-life-politics?p=1505033#post1505033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Weirdly as a left winger I tend to percieve it as left wing. If anything this makes it more scary rather than less.</div> </div> </div> </div>That could possibly be the case for the NWO, Progenitors, and maybe Iteration X, but I don't see how anyone could read the Syndicate as left-wing. Their whole source of magic is private accumulation. The Void Engineers are weird since they are both the most explicitly militaristic and imperial in their logic, but also written as being willing to co-operate with the Traditions and Covenants the most. Again, that's just an example of how these things really can't be read as one-to-one representatives of IRL politics. Hell the lack of political cohesion in the Technocracy outside of their general support for liberal market governance is probably the closest thing to our reality where there are basically no cohesive political projects anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-11T19:58:28-08:00","id":1505155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1504566-in-your-opinion-is-mage-too-attached-to-real-life-politics?p=1505033#post1505033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Weirdly as a left winger I tend to percieve it as left wing. If anything this makes it more scary rather than less.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m a right winger and I\u2019ve always seen the Technocracy as being left wing. Almost like an Alex Jones style conspiracy theory. I could also see them from the perspective of the Technocracy controlling both sides of the establishment with the New World Order pushing the mainstream left and the Syndicate pushing the mainstream right, with the extremes (or those not fitting into the false binary) falling outside of their purview.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-11T20:05:42-08:00","id":1505156,"title":"","content":"\u2026which puts an interesting spin on the \u201cimpending Technocratic civil war\u201d that the Convention Books described which was built around the NWO and the Syndicate being polarized against each other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-12T18:21:47-07:00","id":1505217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1504566-in-your-opinion-is-mage-too-attached-to-real-life-politics?p=1505015#post1505015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The flip side of this is that Mage factions tend to get painted as being for whatever the readers think the group they represent is for, baggage and all. No one blinks an eye at magical healthcare and faith healing in Dungeons and Dragons. In Mage, the factions that practice strange medicine tend to get lumped in with quacks and con artists even though the Mages can make it work and are trying to make it work for everyone. In a similar way the Technocracy is often painted as wanting high healthcare costs or global warming or other anxieties of the modern world, when that is not necessarily true (it might be, but only if it makes for a good story).</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine the Progenitors would like universal access to healthcare. If not for the ability to help more people, then because jumping through hoops of privatized healthcare and insurance is <i>a pain in the ass</i> that also costs way more. There are probably also a lot of other Technocrats who'd love things to be done about Climate Change and other systemic issues.<br /> <br /> The main problem is that Union is also married to the interests of the Syndicate, the most unapologetically Capitalist group in Mage, if not WoD in general. Only Pentex comes close, and even then not by much. &quot;Capitalism&quot; effectively IS the Syndicate's Paradigm. Moreover, even at their most egalitarian, the Syndicate are on record as believing 100% in the idea that change isn't really possible because &quot;people don't want it, they just want comfort&quot;, a Neo-liberal &quot;we are at the end of history&quot; sentiment if I ever saw it.<br /> <br /> Like, the Technocracy as a whole probably won't go in for power being distributed to the masses in a grassroots fashion. The Union is solidly about centralized authority and hierarchical decision-making processes. Their whole deal is &quot;to protect humanity from itself, create a single Consensus that WE control&quot;. At the same time, their desire for making that centralized world as good for people as possible, or even livable, is greatly held back by the Syndicate's desire to protect Capital and its systems of exploitation. Indeed, that them having great political power within the Union as a result of holding the purse-strings is only relevant BECAUSE they perpetuate a system where wealth pools into the hands of a minority, and force everyone else to deal in money to get anything done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 03-12-2023, 09:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-13T01:06:49-07:00","id":1505233,"title":"","content":"In my opinion, the game is not enough attached to real world issue to my own sake and I tend to bring more real life content in my games. I run a campaign when my players tempered with berlin's wall events and tian'anmen's event too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8571-laurange7","name":"Laurange7","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-13T11:21:32-07:00","id":1505261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1504566-in-your-opinion-is-mage-too-attached-to-real-life-politics?p=1505217#post1505217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like, the Technocracy as a whole probably won't go in for power being distributed to the masses in a grassroots fashion. The Union is solidly about centralized authority and hierarchical decision-making processes. Their whole deal is &quot;to protect humanity from itself, create a single Consensus that WE control&quot;. At the same time, their desire for making that centralized world as good for people as possible, or even livable, is greatly held back by the Syndicate's desire to protect Capital and its systems of exploitation. Indeed, that them having great political power within the Union as a result of holding the purse-strings is only relevant BECAUSE they perpetuate a system where wealth pools into the hands of a minority, and force everyone else to deal in money to get anything done.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Technocracy's goals are greatly held back by the inherent conflict of just about all their goals. They want absolute control that somehow still preserves free will. They want to change what it means to be human in the name of defending humanity. They want to manipulate people at every level while somehow still allowing meaningful variance and individuality. The Syndicate's methods are only one in a long list of paradoxes that make up the Technocracy's vision. All of them fail on some fundamental level and will continue to fail unless the world is somehow dramatically reshaped. That's why we often say that the Technocracy is working towards a form of Mass Ascension. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-13T22:20:56-07:00","id":1505285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1504566-in-your-opinion-is-mage-too-attached-to-real-life-politics?p=1505217#post1505217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I imagine the Progenitors would like universal access to healthcare. If not for the ability to help more people, then because jumping through hoops of privatized healthcare and insurance is <i>a pain in the ass</i> that also costs way more. There are probably also a lot of other Technocrats who'd love things to be done about Climate Change and other systemic issues.<br /> <br /> The main problem is that Union is also married to the interests of the Syndicate, the most unapologetically Capitalist group in Mage, if not WoD in general. Only Pentex comes close, and even then not by much. &quot;Capitalism&quot; effectively IS the Syndicate's Paradigm. Moreover, even at their most egalitarian, the Syndicate are on record as believing 100% in the idea that change isn't really possible because &quot;people don't want it, they just want comfort&quot;, a Neo-liberal &quot;we are at the end of history&quot; sentiment if I ever saw it.<br /> <br /> Like, the Technocracy as a whole probably won't go in for power being distributed to the masses in a grassroots fashion. The Union is solidly about centralized authority and hierarchical decision-making processes. Their whole deal is &quot;to protect humanity from itself, create a single Consensus that WE control&quot;. At the same time, their desire for making that centralized world as good for people as possible, or even livable, is greatly held back by the Syndicate's desire to protect Capital and its systems of exploitation. Indeed, that them having great political power within the Union as a result of holding the purse-strings is only relevant BECAUSE they perpetuate a system where wealth pools into the hands of a minority, and force everyone else to deal in money to get anything done.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which, to me, raises an interesting question: is the Syndicate for or against Anti-Trust laws? Anti-Trust laws restrict capitalism in the short-term, but they do so with the intent of preserving capitalism in the long term by preventing capitalism from transforming into feudalism. Once a handful of people win the capitalist race, the rise of monopolies and oligopolies destroys capitalism. Capitalism is always on the verge of suicide, which anti-trust laws prevent. But, again, they do so my restricting capitalism. So which side would the Syndicate be on?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-13T23:59:05-07:00","id":1505288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1504566-in-your-opinion-is-mage-too-attached-to-real-life-politics?p=1505285#post1505285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which, to me, raises an interesting question: is the Syndicate for or against Anti-Trust laws? Anti-Trust laws restrict capitalism in the short-term, but they do so with the intent of preserving capitalism in the long term by preventing capitalism from transforming into feudalism. Once a handful of people win the capitalist race, the rise of monopolies and oligopolies destroys capitalism. Capitalism is always on the verge of suicide, which anti-trust laws prevent. But, again, they do so my restricting capitalism. So which side would the Syndicate be on?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Could be an obvious source of factionalism in the syndicate. Thinking on it you could probably run groups within the syndicate with different economic models than neo liberalism, maybe even unionist or socialist members.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-14T00:43:16-07:00","id":1505291,"title":"","content":"The Syndicate are fundamentally economists, and economics is the study of incentive-structures. Incentive structures can be difficult to balance. For example, back in the day the Vietnamese government tried to incentivize the killing of rats by offering a bounty on rat-tails. The populace then proceeded to farm rats for their tails, chopping them off and then releasing the tailless but alive rats to bred. The rat population became worse than ever.<br /> <br /> Setting up incentive structures can be deceptively complicated. Set up a competition based incentive structure, and the first winners attempt to shut the door to the top behind them, forming monopolies and oligopolies that destroy the very system they were intended to serve. Set up a bureaucratic economic system, and the bureaucrats are incentivized to favor themselves, their families, and friends, to fudge economic numbers, and to erode any method of supervision and transparency that might threaten their position.<br /> <br /> Really, much more of the Syndicate fluff should be about dealing with the complexity of incentive structures, and less about pure cash.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-14T04:33:51-07:00","id":1505307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1504566-in-your-opinion-is-mage-too-attached-to-real-life-politics?p=1505261#post1505261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Technocracy's goals are greatly held back by the inherent conflict of just about all their goals. They want absolute control that somehow still preserves free will. They want to change what it means to be human in the name of defending humanity. They want to manipulate people at every level while somehow still allowing meaningful variance and individuality. The Syndicate's methods are only one in a long list of paradoxes that make up the Technocracy's vision. All of them fail on some fundamental level and will continue to fail unless the world is somehow dramatically reshaped. That's why we often say that the Technocracy is working towards a form of Mass Ascension.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>There are many Enlightened Scientists - not neccesirely idealists or optimists - that do not follow the priorities and goals of these possibly corrupt and self-serving Technocrats. These more positive and reasonable Technocrats definitely very often have the decision-making capability and the power or the vision to influence organisations and events.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-14T06:51:39-07:00","id":1505312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1504566-in-your-opinion-is-mage-too-attached-to-real-life-politics?p=1505288#post1505288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could be an obvious source of factionalism in the syndicate. Thinking on it you could probably run groups within the syndicate with different economic models than neo liberalism, maybe even unionist or socialist members.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately, their book it's very damning against such divergent members having any voice. It pretty much says that the Syndicate allows &quot;socialists&quot; to go rogue and then return after whatever they tried *doesn't work* (OR they become Etherites like that one example in the Etherite book?). I guess one could say the narrator it's IOC and biased, but it's not like there's any real OOC that says otherwise - heck, it's even implied that PU related to public structures it's the purview of the NWO.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> I think it's all rather childish. It's on the same level of &quot;Socialism it's when the goverment does stuff&quot;, but &quot;leftist version&quot;. The history of Capitalism - including liberalism - it's mirred with political intervention, The market it's not <i>free </i>anywhere, and was never <i>free</i>. It's specially clear when you live under the yoke of the IMF &quot;recommendations&quot;, more than proffiting from it's deals. Or when &quot;liberalism&quot; was forced onto you by a military goverment...<br /> <br /> I don't buy that divide between &quot;goverment regulations&quot; and &quot;capitalism&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">once a handful of people win the capitalist race, the rise of monopolies and oligopolies destroys capitalism.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that's the case, then Capitalism it's dead or at least dying. The global economy it's dominated by very few entities thta have clear areas where they excert enormous power (like, look at the pharmaceutical industry). And since a lobying oligarchy building monopolies and monopsonies was the way the world worked since the India Companies, I would wonder if Capitalism was ever dominant in the first place...<br /> <br /> And as per the Syndicate. The book higligths a strong posture against goverment intervention, so I guess they're against anty-trust? But that may be just the narrator being unreliable. And, unlike the previous case this is more likely because not ALL the Syndicate it's against the NWO (at least one faction it's building bridges), but the narrator it's against them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 03-14-2023, 09:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-14T12:49:41-07:00","id":1505360,"title":"","content":"There's a tension between Capitalism-as-System and Capitalism-as-Ideology. The Ideology of Capitalism - the one sold to the public to trick them into accepting their exploitation - is that small numbers of people owning the means of production is good because Competition. But as a policy matter, as an outgrowth of how Capitalism works when unfettered, it inevitably trends to Monopoly. Capitalism is, by its nature, ANTI-Competition. It will get as close to Feudalism as it is allowed to. That's not a bug, but a <i>Feature</i>. It's why the wealthy and powerful adopted it as a system in the wake of violent revolt against Feudal structures.<br /> <br /> One of the greatest deceptions of the Neo-Liberal order has been convincing people that it and Capitalism are non-ideological. When in fact, it's as much a measure of Faith as any that came before it.<br /> <br /> Ergo, while there's plenty of economists among the Syndicate, they are economists working within a paradigm (and Paradigm) fundamentally wedded to Capitalist power structures. It's a cancer that consumes and recuperates everything, up to and including criticisms of Capitalism. There are many Syndicate economists who, in a different reality, might have been using the same Hypereconomics to argue for non-Capitalist economic modes. As it stands, they're working within an Ideological framework centered around Capitalism, just as Celestial Chorusters work within a Monotheistic framework, and the Order of Hermes works within a Hermetic framework. They are as much motivated by Ideology as anyone.<br /> <br /> Where internal differences may exist depends entirely on how much an individual Syndic believes that Ideology, and how much they acknowledge that it's a <i>scam</i> made to maintain existing power structures. The former operate under the belief that if they just do Capitalism hard enough, all its shortcomings will iron themselves out. That if they get enough people believing in Competition and Bootstraps, Competition will happen and people will actually elevate themselves through hard work.<br /> <br /> The latter know that's not really the point, and it's all about keeping the Sleepers under control. That they make loads of money in the process is just a fringe benefit, you see. Trust them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-14T15:00:49-07:00","id":1505377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1504566-in-your-opinion-is-mage-too-attached-to-real-life-politics?p=1505360#post1505360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a tension between Capitalism-as-System and Capitalism-as-Ideology. The Ideology of Capitalism - the one sold to the public to trick them into accepting their exploitation - is that small numbers of people owning the means of production is good because Competition. But as a policy matter, as an outgrowth of how Capitalism works when unfettered, it inevitably trends to Monopoly. Capitalism is, by its nature, ANTI-Competition. It will get as close to Feudalism as it is allowed to. That's not a bug, but a <i>Feature</i>. It's why the wealthy and powerful adopted it as a system in the wake of violent revolt against Feudal structures.<br /> <br /> One of the greatest deceptions of the Neo-Liberal order has been convincing people that it and Capitalism are non-ideological. When in fact, it's as much a measure of Faith as any that came before it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's a very reductionist take. Especially considering what you just described is laissez-faire, a sub-sect of capitalist ideology that is not capitalism as a whole for the same reason stalinism isn't communism as a whole.<br /> <br /> Like any economic and political ideology, there is Waaay more nuance, differing perspectives, faction in-fighting, outside manipulation, straight-up lies/propaganda, and complicated historical context than can be put in a simple black-and-white Us-VS-Them summary(which are nearly always very wrong in any context anyway).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-14T17:55:23-07:00","id":1505397,"title":"","content":"\u2026and now, <i>this thread</i> is veering into being about politics instead of being about whether or not <b>Mage</b> is excessively about politics.<br /> <br /> Because regardless about whether or not, say, Bluecho's description of capitalism is true in the real world, there's the question of whether or not it's true in <b>Mage</b>'s <i>\u201creality is influenced by peoples' beliefs\u201d</i> setting. And getting back on topic, <b>Mage</b>'s writers have the weird, but understandable, tendency to treat physical phenomena as considerably more mutable than matters rooted in peoples' behavior: the so-called \u201chard sciences\u201d (physics, chemistry, geology, astronomy, etc.) are flexible in the published <b>Mage</b> setting, while the so-called \u201csoft sciences\u201d (psychology, sociology, economics, political theory, etc.) are immutable in the published <b>Mage</b> setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-15T05:51:13-07:00","id":1505426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1504566-in-your-opinion-is-mage-too-attached-to-real-life-politics?p=1505397#post1505397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026and now, <i>this thread</i> is veering into being about politics instead of being about whether or not <b>Mage</b> is excessively about politics.<br /> <br /> Because regardless about whether or not, say, Bluecho's description of capitalism is true in the real world, there's the question of whether or not it's true in <b>Mage</b>'s <i>\u201creality is influenced by peoples' beliefs\u201d</i> setting. And getting back on topic, <b>Mage</b>'s writers have the weird, but understandable, tendency to treat physical phenomena as considerably more mutable than matters rooted in peoples' behavior: the so-called \u201chard sciences\u201d (physics, chemistry, geology, astronomy, etc.) are flexible in the published <b>Mage</b> setting, while the so-called \u201csoft sciences\u201d (psychology, sociology, economics, political theory, etc.) are immutable in the published <b>Mage</b> setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I'm fond of pointing out. Mage posits that physical reality is mutable, it never actually makes the claim that moral reality is as well. Indeed, Mages don't act like this is true. They don't try to cast spells to change morality within the local area. They don't act like they are currently in the wrong but will be in the right if they change enough minds. <br /> <br /> As for the soft sciences, they tend to be studies of human systems. Changing them at any kind of important level requires changing human nature. While its never directly stated, there's a tacit assumption that the Consensus does not change itself. Most people in the WoD believe that reality is unchanging, but the Consensus still alters it. So while there are plenty of mind control and manipulation effects, actual changes to human nature are the stuff of Mass Ascension.<br /> <br /> We really wouldn't want it any other way, either. Mage is supposed to be about motives and stakes we at the table understand. Change too much about humanity and we remove that connection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-15T06:51:22-07:00","id":1505428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1504566-in-your-opinion-is-mage-too-attached-to-real-life-politics?p=1505360#post1505360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> There are many Syndicate economists who, in a different reality, might have been using the same Hypereconomics to argue for non-Capitalist economic modes.</div> </div> </div> </div>There might as well be many Syndicate Technocrats - possibly from Asian, African, and South American countries, in particular - who argue for arrangements and types of economies and trade which are not capitalist. Also there might be Technocrats from other Conventions that support this kind of viewpoints and methods.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-15T07:48:58-07:00","id":1505431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1504566-in-your-opinion-is-mage-too-attached-to-real-life-politics?p=1505397#post1505397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because regardless about whether or not, say, Bluecho's description of capitalism is true in the real world, there's the question of whether or not it's true in <b>Mage</b>'s <i>\u201creality is influenced by peoples' beliefs\u201d</i> setting</div> </div> </div> </div>In general WoD setting tries to mimick the real world. This is why \u201creality is influenced by peoples' beliefs\u201d it's so often curbed by the acclaration that water it's wet, Earth isn't flat, and gravity functions more or less as expected. In all editions after the 1rst, it's unlikely the Consensus can alter this to a big extent. But even if it *could*, the fact of the matter it's that *now* things work like this. Physical laws may be *sus*, but they work (at least at a surface level) akin to what we imagine about our real world at the moment we enter the setting with our PCs.<br /> <br /> In a similar vein. Yes, I would say Capitalism functions more or less like what Bluecho describes. The wolrd at large it's still ruled by monopolies, monopsonies, and oligarchies in the WoD (the world would look *very* different if that wasn't the case)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the so-called \u201chard sciences\u201d (physics, chemistry, geology, astronomy, etc.) are flexible in the published <b>Mage</b> setting, while the so-called \u201csoft sciences\u201d (psychology, sociology, economics, political theory, etc.) are immutable in the published <b>Mage</b> setting\u200b </div> </div> </div>Immutable seems too strong a word...<br /> <br /> I think both you and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a> have a point in that Magick(tm) can't change &quot;human nature&quot;. But the thing is... I would argue we don't know what &quot;human nature&quot; is<i> at all</i>. The reason why these scences are called &quot;soft&quot; it's because there's various different and contradictory theories about how all of this work. So, what &quot;immutable law&quot; would you fail to change?<br /> <br /> Example: SO, you say mages can change material reality but not human concepts. OK. But what if humanity changes their concepts indirectly by mages changing said material reality?. Even if we don't go full &quot;materialism&quot;, I don't think it's preposterous to say that when your world changes drastically (as it happens a lot of times: Just see war, poverty, sickeness ... or, why not, prosperity, technological advance...), your worldviews do tend to shake. Unless mages *can't* change the world at all, they should be able to change human systems, just not as a single big ritual (that would be impossible anyhow because of the amount of successes that would be required to afect a majority on the planet - which makes me wonder if it's even necessary to rule that human concepts can't be changed trough magick).<br /> The end results will be hard to predict, yes, but that's not because of any inherent immutability of human nature - it's simply that such large scale projects have a lot of moving parts, and you can't Time 2 all of them...still mage &quot;social scientists&quot; would be significantly better than humans at predicting these things, I would think.<br /> <br /> On a more political vein,<b> human nature</b> it's often used as an excuse for the way Capitalism as a system, with all it's flaws, it's more or less (as Thanos would say) &quot;inevitable&quot;. I don't think this is a good argument. I don't want to derail the thread arguing about this. And also I don't think this is what anyone it's saying (yet), But I do think it's important, due to the general mood of the thread,to at least mention this:<br /> We don't know a whole lot of hard truths about human nature, but it's easy to argue that &quot;Capitalism&quot; isn't hardcoded on it as a law that we &quot;must&quot; argue &quot;mages can't change for the sake of the setting&quot;. It's not even an entirely &quot;humanist&quot; phenomena: The way technology works was necessary for it's inception, and the way geopolitics and military work it's in no small way favoring it's sustenance. If you think Technocracy has a hand on any of these, then they have a hand on the system as well<br /> Finally, on the Doylist side, if it's something any teenager can dream to either &quot;fix&quot; or &quot;end&quot;, I would want my RPG about politics, philosopy and magick to allow me a venue to go that way w/o needing to go so far as to say it's comparable to an objective that may not even exist, and if it does it would be <i>harder </i>than both winning the Ascencion War and making a new Technological Revolution :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-15T07:54:09-07:00","id":1505432,"title":"","content":"Loving where the thread is going. Makes me wonder if there has been a critical reading group that read Mage the Ascension along with something like Wallersteins World Systems Theory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-16T06:10:16-07:00","id":1505485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1504566-in-your-opinion-is-mage-too-attached-to-real-life-politics?p=1505431#post1505431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Immutable seems too strong a word...<br /> <br /> I think both you and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a> have a point in that Magick(tm) can't change &quot;human nature&quot;. But the thing is... I would argue we don't know what &quot;human nature&quot; is<i> at all</i>. The reason why these scences are called &quot;soft&quot; it's because there's various different and contradictory theories about how all of this work. So, what &quot;immutable law&quot; would you fail to change?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is important to differentiate between explanations and the things they explain; between the 'why' and the 'what.' It is the 'what' that is likely outside the reach of the Consensus.<br /> <br /> Now I certainly agree that human nature is hard to define except in the broad strokes, yet we can still say quite a bit about it. People are going to form bonds and attachments, have a sense of right and wrong, have a sense of fair play, claim ownership, claim belonging, have an inner life, feel pride and shame and compassion and injury, form opinions and customs and beliefs, seek to communicate, etc. etc. These are the kind of things that cannot be transformed, truncated, or removed.<br /> <br /> *This list is not exhaustive and focuses on the behavioral over the spiritual though those should be present too, and Mage assumes such.<br /> <br /> Now the degree to which these elements are expressed in a culture can change. Theories for why people are the way they are can change. Governments, cultures, economics can change. Those are all on the table in the Ascension War. The underlying human nature would not change, even when denied.. That's what gives the appearance that the soft sciences are immutable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1504566-in-your-opinion-is-mage-too-attached-to-real-life-politics?p=1505431#post1505431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a more political vein,<b> human nature</b> it's often used as an excuse for the way Capitalism as a system, with all it's flaws, it's more or less (as Thanos would say) &quot;inevitable&quot;. I don't think this is a good argument. I don't want to derail the thread arguing about this. And also I don't think this is what anyone it's saying (yet), But I do think it's important, due to the general mood of the thread,to at least mention this:</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is one of definition; Capitalism is a hazy term. There are definitions that encompass most human action throughout history and Capitalism in that sense is likely inevitable. There are likewise definitions that mostly describe our modern economic systems, and those forms are anything but inevitable. That's why some people can describe Capitalism as a natural extention of human nature and others can describe it as inevitably violating human dignity and each group will look at the other as if they are crazy.<br /> <br /> The solution in most cases is to define terms, but in this case that likely would derail the thread.<br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 03-16-2023, 09:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-21T17:50:38-07:00","id":1506094,"title":"","content":"A simple answer to the topic is, mages are human and human politics can effect them, so they are going to have an interest in politics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-21T18:51:58-07:00","id":1506102,"title":"","content":"Just note that that exact same argument can apply to vampires, save only for the \u201cthey are human\u201d part.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-23T18:25:08-07:00","id":1506281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1504566-in-your-opinion-is-mage-too-attached-to-real-life-politics?p=1505018#post1505018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that's quite correct and it's been something I wanted to point out before the topic spun out of control. Mage is a perfect mirror to hold up against ourselves and our perceptions of the World.<br /> <br /> Mage is about belief, faith and fighting for them. There is a core conflict between freedom, autocracy and destructive nihilism presented through a punky lens that claims that the youth will make it all better... Until they turn into the old.<br /> <br /> Everything else is brought to the table by the people discussing and playing the game. It's not a mirror of our world, it's a mirror of ourselves.<br /> <br /> This is also what makes discussing mage incredibly infuriating because half the time you are not really discussing mage - you are discussing your own ethics and worldviews and when people disagree with you on those you end up arguing.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I personally thing that this theme went too far from the very beginning of mage.<br /> Maybe i am far too cynical of human nature, but i think that in reality a lot of mages would be interested in, say, being able to cast paradox-free fireballs rather than, say, solving world hunger.<br /> Did it never strike anyone weird that almost every single mage was (implicitly) interested in ascension? Think long and hard about the religion concepts of Nirvana, moksha, Theosis, the real thing, not the Hollywood version of it.<br /> Are you dead certain that you want to &quot;ascend&quot;?<br /> Mage, in my view, has always been way in the idealistic side. It is as if its inclusion in the wod was a coincidence.<br /> Like, i don't know, what is the average humanity rating of a vampire? 5? Then maybe for mages it would be 6 rather than, say, 7.<br /> <br /> <br /> Its part of the reason i find the existence of the seers of the thrones in Awakening quite realistic. Yes, some people would join the &quot;asshole&quot; faction.<br /> It is as if there is a big gap between &quot;normal person&quot; and &quot;nephandi&quot; that is not really present in game<br /> Its part of the reason i always saw the technocrats as somewhat goodish, think of a member of control in the year 2000. He has been alive since the year 1000. What has he gained, personally?<br /> (That he can actually use, mind you). I am not saying there is no cynicism in the union(god there is), just not enough that they, as a collective, would stop caring.<br /> Because, lets face it, most of us, in real life, would probably vote Technocracy in the elections<br /> <br /> And i suppose this answers my original question. The writers presume that, essentially, the ring of gyges is wrong.<br /> The other responses are also correct i think. Mage focusing so much on identity politics made it a lot more visceral. It is as if &quot;mages are human&quot; made the writers forget all about the world of darkness.<br /> <br /> I am also reiterating that like i said in the beginning, i was not referring to race/sex/sexuality/etc* in and of itself, but rather the fact that many elements in the game seemed to be representations<br /> or outright caricatures of organizations that the writers hated on a personal level. So, Caeron Mustai probably represented the rotten part of politics and thus we &quot;had&quot; to be against him<br /> <br /> I still believe that some of the writers seemed to be very much afraid that we would draw the wrong conclusions in a way that Vampire or even Werewolf writers would not<br /> <br /> Well, that and the fact that someone really hated Bill Clinton back then. I know i've said it before, but i repeat that the elder vs young wars did not make much sense in mage<br /> Your Elders are not telling you that you can never see your family again. Fuck, you are not even necessarily prohibited from changing your tradition(unlike clans). Nobody will stop you from making children, or &quot;embracing&quot; new mages. In fact, they actively want you to do so. You don't need diablerie to advance. There is no right of hospitality. You can go wherever the hell you want.<br /> Nobody will tell you anything about it for the most part. Even &quot;Domain&quot; amongst mages is more subtle. You are not literally banned from competing in certain industries.<br /> I could go on and on.<br /> <br /> *I actually like the fact that these elements are represented. I merely believe that they are oftentimes presented in a very strawman fashion. (Such as the idea that future hermetic councilor literally insulted have the American Dreamspeakers into leaving or making mages even MORE racist than the people of their time).<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-23T20:28:14-07:00","id":1506285,"title":"","content":"The interviews of the writers for <b>Lore of the Traditions</b> provides some interesting insight into this: that book was written from the perspective of \u201chow can we present the Traditions as The Good Guys\u2122\u201d? In particular, the book is about presenting each Tradition in the modern era, with the idea being that they've all reflected on their past failings and jettisoned the Bad Stuff that had been bogging them down. I noticed several times in the interviews comments along the lines of, say, \u201creal-world Wicca has some problems with mysandry; but that would make the Verbena look bad, so I had to dance around it\u201d. (I don't know if I got that particular example exactly right; but the overall attitude represented by it was very much present in the interviews.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-29T14:14:19-07:00","id":1506871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1504566-in-your-opinion-is-mage-too-attached-to-real-life-politics?p=1506285#post1506285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The interviews of the writers for <b>Lore of the Traditions</b> provides some interesting insight into this: that book was written from the perspective of \u201chow can we present the Traditions as The Good Guys\u2122\u201d? In particular, the book is about presenting each Tradition in the modern era, with the idea being that they've all reflected on their past failings and jettisoned the Bad Stuff that had been bogging them down. I noticed several times in the interviews comments along the lines of, say, \u201creal-world Wicca has some problems with mysandry; but that would make the Verbena look bad, so I had to dance around it\u201d. (I don't know if I got that particular example exactly right; but the overall attitude represented by it was very much present in the interviews.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, at least I now know I am not paranoid.<br /> I get the impression that the reason the rest of the wod is not written like that is just a happy coincidence. <br /> I am almost afraid to ask how vampire would look like if it debuted today <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-11T02:54:41-07:00","id":1508011,"title":"","content":"Personally I prefer a warts and all mindset. It's supposed to be a gritty world with serious problems even in the good guy camp.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-11T06:14:44-07:00","id":1508024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1504566-in-your-opinion-is-mage-too-attached-to-real-life-politics?p=1508011#post1508011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I prefer a warts and all mindset. It's supposed to be a gritty world with serious problems even in the good guy camp.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That would require people on the internet to differentiate between portrayal of a fictional group and endorsement of abhorrent behavior.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-11T08:13:44-07:00","id":1508034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1504566-in-your-opinion-is-mage-too-attached-to-real-life-politics?p=1508024#post1508024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That would require people on the internet to differentiate between portrayal of a fictional group and endorsement of abhorrent behavior.</div> </div> </div> </div>The majority can. However, Jumping on the &quot;scandle&quot; bandwagon is more fun and anonymity has a way of shielding people from consequences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-12T01:39:52-07:00","id":1508128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1504566-in-your-opinion-is-mage-too-attached-to-real-life-politics?p=1508011#post1508011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I prefer a warts and all mindset. It's supposed to be a gritty world with serious problems even in the good guy camp.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, i really wish i could rename this thread &quot; Is mage's assumptions about how people and groups act way too Idealistic?&quot; <br /> <br /> I have a BA in history, and getting my master's in International relations, with a focus on the realist tradition. I also happen to have something of a layman's interest in the ways that power affects people.<br /> Needless to say, i live a very depressing life, lmao. Given that this is the wod, i think i feel kinda justified in seeing the glass half empty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}